      "text": "Let's solve the given expression step-by-step.\n\nThe expression we need to compute is:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{\\cos 80^\\circ} - \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sin 80^\\circ}.\n\\]\n\nFirst, we can combine the terms over a common denominator:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{\\sin 80^\\circ - \\sqrt{3} \\cos 80^\\circ}{\\cos 80^\\circ \\sin 80^\\circ}.\n\\]\n\nWe can further simplify the numerator. Notice that:\n\n\\[\n\\sin 80^\\circ - \\sqrt{3} \\cos 80^\\circ = 2 \\left( \\frac{1}{2} \\sin 80^\\circ - \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\cos 80^\\circ \\right).\n\\]\n\nUsing the angle subtraction identity for sine, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{2} \\sin 80^\\circ - \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\cos 80^\\circ = \\sin (80^\\circ - 60^\\circ) = \\sin 20^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nSo the expression simplifies to:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{2 \\sin 20^\\circ}{\\cos 80^\\circ \\sin 80^\\circ}.\n\\]\n\nWe can use the double-angle identity for sine, \\(\\sin 2A = 2 \\sin A \\cos A\\), to simplify further:\n\n\\[\n\\sin 20^\\circ = 2 \\sin 80^\\circ \\cos 80^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nThus, the numerator becomes:\n\n\\[\n2 \\sin 20^\\circ = 2 \\cdot 2 \\sin 80^\\circ \\cos 80^\\circ = 4 \\sin 80^\\circ \\cos 80^\\circ.\n\\]\n\nSo the expression now is:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{4 \\sin 80^\\circ \\cos 80^\\circ}{\\cos 80^\\circ \\sin 80^\\circ} = 4.\n\\]\n\nSo the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{4}\n\\]\n\nLet's verify this using Python.\n```python\nimport math\r\n\r\n# Convert degrees to radians\r\nangle_deg = 80\r\nangle_rad = math.radians(angle_deg)\r\n\r\n# Compute the expression\r\nnumerator = 1 / math.cos(angle_rad) - math.sqrt(3) / math.sin(angle_rad)\r\ndenominator = math.cos(angle_rad) * math.sin(angle_rad)\r\nresult = numerator / denominator\r\n\r\nprint(result)\n```",
